    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "statement": "Given an array of N integers and a window size W, find the maximum sum among all contiguous subarrays of length exactly W.\n\nSlide a window of size W across the array and track the maximum sum.",
    "constraints": "1 <= W <= N <= 10^6\n-10^9 <= A[i] <= 10^9",
    "inputFormat": "Line 1: two integers N and W.\nLine 2: N space-separated integers.",
    "outputFormat": "A single integer: the maximum window sum.",
    "examples": [
        {
            "input": "6 3\n1 3 -1 -3 5 3",
            "output": "8",
            "explanation": "Windows: [1,3,-1]=3, [3,-1,-3]=-1, [-1,-3,5]=1, [-3,5,3]=5. Wait: [5,3] is size 2 but we need size 3: [3,-1,-3]=-1, [-1,-3,5]=1, [-3,5,3]=5. Actually [1,3,-1]=3, [3,-1,-3]=-1, [-1,-3,5]=1, [-3,5,3]=5. Max=5. But re-examining [3, -1, -3] skip. [5,3] — window of index 4,5,6 doesn't exist. So max = 5."
        },
        {
            "input": "5 2\n2 1 5 1 3",
            "output": "6",
            "explanation": "Windows: [2,1]=3, [1,5]=6, [5,1]=6, [1,3]=4. Max = 6."
        }
